# Supply-chain hardening: never execute dependency lifecycle scripts
# (preinstall/install/postinstall/prepare) at install time. A malicious or
# compromised package version then cannot run code on a developer machine or CI
# before anyone reviews it.
#
# No dependency here genuinely needs an install script:
#   - esbuild (via tsx): ships prebuilt platform packages
#     (@esbuild/linux-x64, ...). Its postinstall only locates/downloads a
#     binary; the JS entry resolves the platform package directly.
#   - unrs-resolver (via eslint): ships prebuilt
#     @unrs/resolver-binding-* platform packages. Its postinstall is a
#     download fallback.
#   - fsevents: macOS-only optional dependency, so it is absent on Linux CI.
#
# If a future dependency genuinely requires an install script, do NOT flip this
# to false globally. Run that one script explicitly with review and record the
# exception in SECURITY.md.
ignore-scripts=true
